# corpus/NOTICES

Every program in `corpus/` is third party work.
It is here because its licence permits redistribution.
This file names the origin, the licence, and the upstream commit of each one.

A program that does not have such a licence does not go in this directory.
The test harness fetches those at run time instead, from a manifest of pinned
hashes, and their bytes are never committed.

## corpus/vb6-code

Origin: https://github.com/tannerhelland/vb6-code
Upstream commit: f2703861b9e6a7ed4acdc6eedb2632ca8903f895
Licence: BSD 2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2018, Tanner Helland
Licence text: `corpus/vb6-code/LICENSE.md`

32 Visual Basic 6 projects with the executable that each one builds.
31 executables, all Standard EXE, all native code, all verified to import
MSVBVM60.

Two kinds of file were left out of this copy.
The sample JPEG images were left out because they are one megabyte and the
gate does not read them.
`Scanner-TWAIN/EZTW32.dll` was left out because it is a third party library
that the upstream author did not write and cannot relicense.
Nothing else was changed.

