## Why these and not others

A sweep of 366 Visual Basic 6 repositories found 120 that hold both source and
an executable.
Only 52 of those carry a licence that permits redistribution.
`.planning/research/CORPUS.md` records the measurement, and names what was
rejected and why.

Microsoft's own VB98 samples are not here.
The Visual Studio 6 licence grants no redistribution right, and the samples
shipped without executables, so they carry no ground truth.
